course: dictionary
lesson: 11723
title: Words about the seasons
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Autumnal means about autumn, or typical of autumn. Autumn is the season between summer and winter, when leaves turn orange and fall, and the air gets cooler. «The park was full of autumnal colours: red, orange and gold.» The colours are the clue: leaves in red, orange and gold look like autumn, so autumnal must mean like autumn.
explain: Autumnal is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you about a noun, such as autumnal colours, an autumnal day or an autumnal wind. You can test your meaning by swapping in autumn: «an autumn day» makes sense, so «an autumnal day» means a day that feels like autumn.
explain: You may also meet autumnal in science. The autumnal equinox is the day in September when day and night are about the same length. «The autumnal equinox came on 22 September.» Here the word still means about autumn, and it names one special point in the season.
fact: Autumnal means about autumn, or typical of autumn.
fact: «Autumnal colours» means the reds, oranges and golds of the leaves.
fact: In the UK and much of the Northern Hemisphere, autumn is roughly September to November.
fact: The autumnal equinox is around 22 or 23 September in the Northern Hemisphere.
fact: Check a new word by swapping in a simple word such as autumn and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The park was full of autumnal colours: red, orange and gold.» What does autumnal mean? | Very hot and sunny | About spring, with new flowers | Very cold and icy | *About autumn, or like autumn
exercise: Mum says, «It's an autumnal evening, so bring a jumper.» Which clue tells you the evening is chilly? | It's | Mum | *Bring a jumper | Evening
exercise: Which of these is most autumnal? | Snowmen in the garden | Ice cream on the beach in July | Blossom on the apple trees in spring | *Crunchy brown leaves falling from the trees
test:
In «the autumnal equinox», what does autumnal tell you? | Linked to the sea | *Linked to autumn | Linked to a football match | Linked to snow
Which sentence uses autumnal correctly? | The children swam in the autumnal sea in July | *The walkers wore scarves against the autumnal chill | The ice cream melted in the autumnal heat | Dad will autumnal the car on Monday
exam: «The woods glowed gold in the autumnal light.» Which word could replace autumnal and keep the same meaning? | *Autumn-like | Summery | Icy | Snowy
